35
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:35,840
Marco, you already told our listeners about one phrase, to dry clean.

36
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:37,320
So dry cleaned.

37
00:01:38,080 --> 00:01:44,960
Alright so that's when you take your clothes to a professional who doesn't only wash them, right?

38
00:01:44,960 --> 00:01:46,240
You don't just put water and soap on it.

39
00:01:46,520 --> 00:01:53,500
They actually put some special chemicals and use special machines to get very hard to remove stains from it.

40
00:01:53,920 --> 00:01:54,920
Exactly.

41
00:01:54,920 --> 00:02:01,330
So this is often what we use when we clean coats or fancy shirts and dresses because you don't want to clean those yourself.

42
00:02:01,360 --> 00:02:02,360
Right.

43
00:02:02,360 --> 00:02:03,150
You can't put those in the washing machine.

44
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:03,550
No.

45
00:02:03,550 --> 00:02:04,850
So this is the dry cleaner.

46
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:06,110
That's the name of the place.

47
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:09,730
And the action, what they do is they dry clean clothes.

48
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:10,390
Okay.

49
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:10,950
Very good.

50
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:13,080
Alright.

51
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:16,640
So we take them to the dry cleaners because we want to remove stains.

52
00:02:16,650 --> 00:02:17,030
Okay.

53
00:02:17,150 --> 00:02:24,030
So a stain is a mark or some color that does not come off, does not go away.

54
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,400
Alright.

55
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:29,130
So for example, sometimes you can have a wine stain.

56
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,360
Oh, wine stains are the worst.

57
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,770
They're red and they never come off.

58
00:02:32,770 --> 00:02:33,770
Or blood stain.

59
00:02:33,930 --> 00:02:34,630
Or blood stain.

60
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
Oh.

61
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Right.

62
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,240
So a stain is a noun but you can also use it as an adjective.

63
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:41,610
My shirt is stained.

64
00:02:42,030 --> 00:02:42,330
Okay.

65
00:02:42,450 --> 00:02:43,490
So it's stained.

66
00:02:44,230 --> 00:02:46,730
My pants are stained and I can't wear them again.

67
00:02:47,080 --> 00:02:49,410
Again, you can also use it as a verb.

68
00:02:49,890 --> 00:02:50,950
I stained my pants.

69
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:51,510
Alright.

70
00:02:52,240 --> 00:02:54,350
So it's a verb, it's a noun and an adjective all in one.

71
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:55,310
Easy to remember.

72
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:59,330
Well, there's another word that's related to this word.

73
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:01,050
We spilled something.

74
00:03:01,250 --> 00:03:01,450
Okay.

75
00:03:01,730 --> 00:03:04,190
So I spilled wine and it stained my shirt.

76
00:03:04,450 --> 00:03:04,750
Okay.

77
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:11,240
So to spill and that means that you took some liquid and you put it onto your clothes.

78
00:03:11,540 --> 00:03:13,340
Or you dropped it and it made a mess.

79
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,600
Okay.

80
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:15,600
So spill.

81
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:16,400
I spilled some milk.

82
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,060
Okay.

83
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:17,360
Spilled.

84
00:03:17,840 --> 00:03:20,240
Now it's pronounced differently from spell, right?

85
00:03:20,720 --> 00:03:20,980
That's right.

86
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:22,880
Spill.

87
00:03:22,880 --> 00:03:23,880
It has an I, spilled.

88
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:24,880
Alright.

89
00:03:24,880 --> 00:03:27,220
Now our next word is also a noun and a verb.

90
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:28,280
To iron.

91
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:32,400
To iron means to make something flat with no lines.

92
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,720
Okay.

93
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,280
To smooth it out.

94
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:38,140
So we use an iron to iron.

95
00:03:38,360 --> 00:03:38,700
Exactly.

96
00:03:39,320 --> 00:03:42,240
It's a metal electronic object.

97
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:43,110
It gets very hot.

98
00:03:43,840 --> 00:03:48,800
So you wash your shirts for example and your shirts are wrinkled because you just washed them.

99
00:03:48,800 --> 00:03:49,670
So you need to iron them.

100
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:51,280
That's right.

101
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:54,170
So you smooth them out, you flatten them with this object, an iron.

102
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,080
Okay.

103
00:03:56,080 --> 00:04:02,070
And well, usually if you take them to the dry cleaners, they will iron them and also starch them.

104
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:02,840
Okay.

105
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:11,680
To starch something means to use some powder or chemical to make something stiff or hard.

106
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:16,400
So the noun or the chemical is also called starch.

107
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:17,160
Exactly.

108
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:20,800
So you think of a shirt with many buttons that a man wears to work.

109
00:04:21,080 --> 00:04:26,260
He has a collar around his neck and that needs to be high and tall.

110
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,260
It can't be flat and wrinkled.

111
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:33,320
And so a dry cleaner will use starch to make sure that this stands up.

112
00:04:33,320 --> 00:04:34,320
Okay.

113
00:04:34,320 --> 00:04:35,320
Very good.

